# Code owners are requested for review automatically; with branch protection,
# their approval is required. The last matching pattern takes precedence.
#
# Security-sensitive paths follow docs/security/09-secure-development-lifecycle.md §2.
# Replace @B-Pine on those paths with the security lead (or a team such as
# @<org>/security) once that role is assigned.

# Default owner
*                               @B-Pine

# Authorisation and permissions
/backend/**/authz/              @B-Pine
**/permissions*                 @B-Pine

# Database migrations (RLS policies are created here)
**/migrations/                  @B-Pine

# Settings and security modules
/backend/config/settings/       @B-Pine
**/settings/                    @B-Pine
**/security/                    @B-Pine
/docs/security/                 @B-Pine
/SECURITY.md                    @B-Pine

# CI/CD, dependency automation and repository protection
/.github/workflows/             @B-Pine
/.github/dependabot.yml         @B-Pine
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @B-Pine

# Containers and infrastructure
Dockerfile                      @B-Pine
*.Dockerfile                    @B-Pine
docker-compose*.yml             @B-Pine
compose*.yml                    @B-Pine
/infra/                         @B-Pine
